{"id": "EUVD-2026-76681", "enisaUuid": "740ea1f8-3089-35bf-a66b-1d0b9a954a1f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nclocksource/drivers/nxp-pit: Fix IRQ leak on cpuhp_setup_state error path\n\nWhen cpuhp_setup_state fails after pit_clockevent_per_cpu_init has\nsuccessfully called request_irq, the error handling jumps directly to\nout_pit_clocksource_unregister without freeing the registered IRQ.\n\nThis leaks the IRQ line and, since kfree(pit) follows, leaves a\ndangling pointer registered as the interrupt handler's dev_id,\npotentially leading to a use-after-free if the IRQ fires afterwards.\n\nFix it by calling pit_clockevent_per_cpu_exit to properly release the\nIRQ before falling through to the existing cleanup chain.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:47:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:22", "baseScore": 7.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d53c29a89a15e56a1797f3ef249955e544782e04", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cdcd861123248e871c2ec2be968b0a1b2a5a34b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/05520e035f8332c8e33f3011b5ca016fde61793d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89769", "GHSA-8vp9-2h56-3438"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00a722c8-2db4-3f53-b9e4-1cb54d457d85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bee33f22d7c30626e711b4900e3f460b6e0e104f <05520e035f8332c8e33f3011b5ca016fde61793d"}, {"id": "0ac3892f-7175-3793-b77a-688173569d4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "169d5c5e-16c9-3ea3-a009-d43a436ebb67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bee33f22d7c30626e711b4900e3f460b6e0e104f <cdcd861123248e871c2ec2be968b0a1b2a5a34b0"}, {"id": "2edf53ed-32fd-3a9a-9039-98b8e938fc25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3fef2d59-bed1-3bcf-a97b-c89a8d264872", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "4e921d65-c8eb-30bd-8806-d62a30fec425", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bee33f22d7c30626e711b4900e3f460b6e0e104f <d53c29a89a15e56a1797f3ef249955e544782e04"}, {"id": "9a941647-48fe-344d-8753-02ff22b3d3b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "e9ba187b-01fe-3834-b7f0-af2514537463", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ccd42acd-78e4-369c-848b-45fc8b346843", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}